Characteristics of XSS
	Code injection where an attacker injects malicious JS into a website so it runs in the browser of other users
	1. Injects JS into trusted website
		Attacker doesn't target the server directly, they target other users visiting the site
	2. Exploits poor input validation / sanitization
		XSS happens because the application does not properly sanitize user input
		The site reflects or stores malicious code and sends it to other users
	3. Steals or manipulates user data
		XSS can be used to:
			Steal session cookies
			Perform actions as the user
